# ClassNames Usage and Conventions

This rule defines how to use the `classNames` package and order Tailwind CSS classes in the project.

## 1. Component Props Pattern

- Import `classNames` from 'classnames' at the top of the file with other third-party imports
- The className prop should be optional (`className?: string`)
- Merge consumer className at the end: `className={classNames('default classes', className)}`

## 2. Breakpoint Order (Mobile-First)

Classes must be ordered from smallest to largest screen size:

1. Base styles (no prefix) - applies to all screen sizes
2. `xs:` → `s:` → `sm:` → `md:` → `m:` → `lg:` → `xl:` → `2xl:`

**Note:** Always verify actual breakpoint names and values from the project's `tailwind.config` file - they may differ from the example above.

## 3. Class Organization

- Group classes by breakpoint in separate strings
- Keep related styles together within each breakpoint group
- Order utility classes logically: layout → spacing → typography → colors → effects
- No trailing commas after the last className argument

## 4. Examples

### Basic Breakpoint Ordering

```typescript
className={classNames(
  'base-style-1 base-style-2',
  'xs:xs-style-1 xs:xs-style-2',
  's:s-style-1 s:s-style-2',
  'sm:sm-style-1 sm:sm-style-2',
  'md:md-style-1 md:md-style-2',
  'm:m-style-1 m:m-style-2',
  'lg:lg-style-1 lg:lg-style-2',
  'xl:xl-style-1 xl:xl-style-2',
  '2xl:2xl-style-1 2xl:2xl-style-2'
)}
```

### Conditional Classes and Passed className Prop

```typescript
type Props = {
  className?: string;
  size?: ButtonSize;
  variant?: ButtonVariant;
};

const Button = ({ children, size = ButtonSize.MEDIUM, variant = ButtonVariant.PRIMARY, className, ...props }) => (
  <button
    className={classNames(
      'block rounded-lg text-center transition',
      'disabled:opacity-50',
      { 'px-3 py-2 text-sm-medium': size === ButtonSize.SMALL },
      { 'px-4 py-3 text-md-medium': size === ButtonSize.MEDIUM },
      { 'bg-orange-500 text-white hover:bg-orange-700': variant === ButtonVariant.PRIMARY },
      { 'outline outline-gray-500 hover:text-orange-500': variant === ButtonVariant.SECONDARY },
      { 'pointer-events-none': Boolean(props?.disabled) },
      className
    )}
    type="button"
    {...props}
  >
    {children}
  </button>
);
```

### Multiple className Props for Sub-elements

```typescript
type Props = {
  title: ReactNode;
  children: ReactNode;
  className?: string;
  headerClassName?: string;
  contentClassName?: string;
};

export const Card: React.FC<Props> = ({
  title,
  children,
  className,
  headerClassName,
  contentClassName,
}) => (
  <div className={classNames('rounded-lg border', className)}>
    <div className={classNames('border-b p-4', headerClassName)}>{title}</div>
    <div className={classNames('p-4', contentClassName)}>{children}</div>
  </div>
);
```

### Shared Styles

```typescript
const Buttons = () => {
  const buttonClassName = classNames(
    'flex w-full shrink-0 items-center justify-center transition-colors',
    'lg:cursor-pointer'
  );

  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <button className={classNames(buttonClassName, 'button-primary')}>
        {/* Content */}
      </button>

      <button className={classNames(buttonClassName, 'button-secondary')}>
        {/* Content */}
      </button>
    </div>
  );
};
```
